  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "What is the value of \\[\\dfrac{2a^{-1}+\\frac{a^{-1}}{2}}{a}\\] when \\(a= \\tfrac{1}{2}?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( \\ 1 \\)",
    "B": "\\( \\ 2 \\)",
    "C": "\\( \\ \\dfrac{5}{2} \\)",
    "D": "\\( \\ 10 \\)",
    "E": "\\( \\ 20 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "A negative exponent of \\(-1\\) means to take the reciprocal. Since \\(a=\\tfrac12\\ne0\\), we have \\(a^{-1}=2\\). Substituting this value gives\n\\[\n\\frac{2(2)+\\frac22}{\\frac12}\n=\\frac{4+1}{\\frac12}\n=5\\cdot2\n=10.\n\\]\nThe value is \\(10\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
